    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d501">

                <pb facs="0695" n="615" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.801/674</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the French Ambassador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Laboulaye</hi>)<anchor n="13" xml:id="d501-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p>The Secretary of State presents his compliments to His Excellency the Ambassador
                    of France and acknowledges the receipt of his note of March 18, 1936, with
                    regard to certain legislation pertaining to shipping (H. R. 112) which was
                    introduced in the House of Representatives January 3, 1935, and upon which
                    hearings are to be held before the Committee on Merchant Marine and Fisheries of
                    the House of Representatives March 24, 1936. The note of the French Government
                    referred to is being transmitted by the Secretary of State to the appropriate
                    agencies of the United States Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1936-03-23">March 23,
                            1936</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d501-f1" n="13" type="source" xml:id="d501-f1-content">
                <p>Similar notes were sent to the missions in Washington of each of the countries
                    which had lodged representations against H. R. 112.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
